<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">National Front (Colombia)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1958">1958</a>–<a href="/years/1974">1974</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-front-czechoslovakia">National Front</a> was a power-sharing agreement in Colombia from 1958 to 1974, under which the Liberal and Conservative parties alternated in the presidency every four years and divided public offices equally. Agreed after the fall of the dictator Gustavo Rojas Pinilla, it ended the partisan bloodshed of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-violencia">La Violencia</a>. Because it shut out other parties, critics blame it for fuelling the rise of leftist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrillas</a>.</p></div>
